# L §4.3: "law cut is allowed and is then written, not defaulted"; the cut is the model's on (L §4.5).
# rate is 1 in 2025 and 2 from 2026-07 (a replace): read at the cut 2026-12-31, 2.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input rate: int

def y: int at reader
  rule base = rate

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 1

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07..
  known 2026-06-01
  replace rate = 2

ask q1: y law cut
=== expect
q1: 2
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
